# Pepto – API, Extensive & Load Testing KT

## Overview
This KT explains post-deployment validation for Pepto and Facade using API testing, extensive testing, and load testing before production release.

## Testing Types
1. API (Sanity) Testing
2. Extensive (Negative) Testing
3. Load & Performance Testing

## API Testing (JMeter)
- Uses common JMX files.
- Separate test groups for:
  - Facade endpoints
  - PDS endpoints
- Update host/IP based on Dev or ITG stack.
- Execute APIs one-by-one initially.
- Validate:
  - HTTP 200 response
  - No pod restarts
  - Logs present in OpenSearch
  - Data landed in S3

## Extensive Testing
- Around ~148 test cases (mainly PDS).
- Sends invalid inputs intentionally.
- Verifies proper 4xx error handling.
- Ensures bad data is rejected safely.

## Pre-Load Test Configuration
- Perform in ITG stack only.
- Set minReplica = maxReplica = 1.
- Disable auto-scaling temporarily.
- Increase max-per-day request limits.
- Ensure instance types match production.

## Load Testing Goals
- Replicate per-pod production traffic.
- Validate CPU, memory, response time (P99).
- Ensure zero/near-zero error rate.

## Load Execution
- Trigger JMeter from remote desktop.
- Run continuously for ~5 days.
- Monitor via Grafana:
  - CPU stability
  - Memory leaks
  - Throughput
  - Response times

## Auto-Scaling Testing
- Increase max replicas gradually.
- Increase load step-by-step.
- Verify pods scale up and down smoothly.

## Success Criteria
- Stable memory and CPU.
- No unexpected restarts.
- Throughput matches baseline.
- P99 within acceptable limits.

## Outcome
This KT ensures confidence that new changes are functionally correct, performance-safe, and production-ready.
